expectation e_susumu_portable_project_memory target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Susumu keeps portable project memory" detail="Susumu should preserve observed evidence, authored expectations, verification results, decisions, and work records in portable artifacts that can be reviewed outside the original source tree.";
expectation e_susumu_scanner_truth_boundary target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Scanner evidence remains distinct from judgment" detail="Susumu should keep scanner-observed facts, deterministic derived findings, human intent, verification reports, decisions, work records, and optional AI drafts visibly separate.";
expectation e_susumu_review_packets target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Review packets are useful standalone artifacts" detail="Susumu should create review packets that include enough artifact, review, source-preview, and next-action context for engineers, stakeholders, and agents to inspect later.";
expectation e_susumu_ci_pr_artifacts target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Pull requests can produce Susumu review artifacts" detail="The repository should demonstrate how CI can generate machine-readable check output, review packets, and standalone HTML review portals for pull requests.";
expectation e_susumu_pages_portal target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Main branch publishes the latest Susumu portal" detail="The repository should demonstrate how the latest Susumu review portal can be published as an always-current static site from CI, using GitHub Pages for open source and the same artifact pattern for internal business portals.";
expectation e_susumu_ai_optional target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="AI assistance stays optional and labeled" detail="Susumu should not require AI keys for core scanning, checking, review packets, or portal export. Optional AI output should be labeled, cited, and reviewable before becoming trusted project memory.";
expectation e_susumu_repo_init target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Projects can start the Susumu way" detail="Susumu should provide a simple repository initialization flow that creates an authored expectations sidecar without requiring users to hand-write the artifact syntax first.";
expectation e_susumu_auto_expectations target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Initialized projects load expectations automatically" detail="When scanning a repository directory, Susumu should automatically merge the repository's expectations.susu sidecar when no explicit expectations file is supplied, so initialized projects follow the Susumu workflow by default.";
expectation e_susumu_review_build target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Daily review builds run in one command" detail="Susumu should provide a single review build command that scans the project, writes the current artifact, records machine-readable check output when requested, creates a review packet, and optionally exports or serves the review portal.";
expectation e_susumu_expectation_support target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Expectations show their supporting evidence" detail="Susumu review packets should summarize each expectation's current support, including whether its target is observed, which verification statuses exist, how much work or decision context is linked, and which gaps remain.";
expectation e_susumu_git_work_support target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Git work can support project expectations" detail="Susumu should be able to connect local Git commits to project-level expectations and export work records from those commits, so expectation support can reflect real repository activity without hand-authored work records.";
expectation e_susumu_easy_daily_cli target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Daily Susumu commands stay simple" detail="Susumu should make normal project review workflows easy to remember and type, using short commands like review, status, open, and git with convention-based files while preserving advanced options for detailed control.";
expectation e_susumu_docs_teach_daily_workflow target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Documentation teaches the daily Susumu workflow" detail="Susumu documentation should introduce the simple human workflow first, explain which files people author and which files Susumu generates, and keep advanced commands discoverable without making them the default path.";
expectation e_susumu_explicit_git_links target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Commits can be explicitly linked to expectations" detail="When Susumu cannot safely infer which expectation a commit supports, users should be able to explicitly link that commit to an expectation and write a work record without rewriting Git history.";
expectation e_susumu_git_suggests_next_links target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Git connection output suggests next links" detail="When Susumu reports unconnected commits, the output should suggest concrete next commands and likely expectation candidates so users can continue the daily workflow without guessing the syntax.";
expectation e_susumu_expectations_are_easy_to_browse target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Expectations are easy to browse and choose" detail="Susumu should provide a simple daily command for listing, searching, and filtering expectation ids so users can quickly choose the right expectation for git links, reviews, and verification work.";
expectation e_susumu_verify_is_easy target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Expectations are easy to verify" detail="Susumu should provide a simple daily command for recording passed, failed, or inconclusive verification evidence against an expectation, so support can become explicit reviewable proof without hand-writing syntax.";
expectation e_susumu_git_link_preserves_multiple_expectations target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Explicit Git links preserve multiple expectations" detail="When a user links the same commit to multiple expectations, Susumu should create stable expectation-specific work records instead of overwriting an earlier link for that commit.";
expectation e_susumu_portal_expectation_ladder target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Portal shows each expectation's evidence ladder" detail="Susumu's review portal should make each expectation's evidence ladder clear, showing observed target evidence, linked work, verification evidence, decision context, review status, and the next suggested action.";
expectation e_susumu_portal_readiness_board target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Portal summarizes expectation readiness" detail="Susumu's review portal should group expectations by readiness so stakeholders can quickly see which expectations are verified, need verification, need linked work, have failed checks, or have missing targets.";
expectation e_susumu_portal_dirty_source_links target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Portal links dirty records to source evidence" detail="Susumu's review portal should surface dirty or stale evidence flags and show nearby syntax-highlighted source when a record or finding has a file location.";
expectation e_susumu_portal_traceability_scroll target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Traceability panes scroll independently" detail="The review portal's traceability page should let users scroll the expectation list and selected evidence detail independently so long expectation lists do not block inspection of the right-hand evidence pane.";
expectation e_susumu_portal_calm_contained_theme target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Portal uses a calm contained default theme" detail="The review portal should use soft, low-glare default colors and keep traceability detail content contained within its card so long ids, code previews, or evidence text do not break the layout.";
expectation e_susumu_portal_brand_config target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Portal branding can be configured" detail="Susumu should let projects brand the generated portal with local configuration for colors, names, and related visual identity without changing the review packet's evidence semantics.";
expectation e_susumu_git_exports_multiple_expectations target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Git work can support multiple expectations" detail="When one commit deterministically supports multiple expectations, Susumu should export separate work records so each expectation receives explicit work support instead of collapsing the commit to a single expectation.";
expectation e_susumu_packet_readiness_queue target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Review packets expose expectation readiness" detail="Susumu review packets should include a machine-readable expectation readiness queue so agents, CI, and portal users can rely on the same readiness buckets and next actions.";
expectation e_susumu_readiness_command target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Readiness is easy to inspect from the CLI" detail="Susumu should provide a simple readiness command that reads the latest review packet and prints expectation readiness counts and next actions, with JSON output for agents and CI.";
expectation e_susumu_readiness_filters target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Readiness can be filtered quickly" detail="Susumu readiness output should support bucket and text filters so humans, agents, and CI can quickly focus on failed, unverified, unsupported, or topic-specific expectations.";
expectation e_susumu_infrastructure_work_kind target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Work records can describe infrastructure changes" detail="Susumu work records should include an infrastructure kind so CI, deployment, hosting, and configuration changes do not have to be mislabeled as implementation or other work.";
expectation e_susumu_modular_cli target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="CLI implementation grows through focused modules" detail="Susumu should keep the command-line surface easy to extend by moving cohesive parsing, routing, and command support code out of the monolithic binary entry point into focused modules with regression coverage.";
expectation e_susumu_compliance_support_stays_honest target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Compliance support stays evidence-oriented and non-certifying" detail="Susumu may help development teams and businesses assemble, inspect, and preserve evidence toward their own compliance processes, but Susumu must never state or imply that a control, regulation, certification, or compliance requirement has been met or will be met. Human and organizational review remain authoritative.";
expectation e_susumu_verification_history_is_append_only target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Verification history is append-only" detail="Supported Susumu commands must preserve prior verification records and represent replacement or retraction as a new record linked to the prior record, while remaining explicit that direct edits to ordinary text files require a later tamper-evidence layer.";
expectation e_susumu_evidence_hashes_are_provider_neutral target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Evidence hashes are provider-neutral and privacy-safe" detail="Susumu should be able to record a content hash for an evidence artifact supplied by any local or CI/CD environment without uploading or copying the artifact contents, while clearly stating that a hash alone does not prove execution, provenance, retention, or compliance.";
expectation e_susumu_provenance_tiers_are_not_compliance_claims target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Provenance tiers never become compliance claims" detail="Susumu should distinguish declared metadata, content-bound evidence, externally authenticated attestations, and human review, while refusing to label any tier as certification or as proof that a control, regulation, or compliance requirement has been met.";
expectation e_susumu_attestation_inputs_remain_untrusted_until_verified target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Attestation inputs remain untrusted until verified" detail="Susumu should parse and inspect provider-neutral attestation envelopes without promoting their issuer, signature, execution, or retention claims to authenticated status until a configured verifier and trust policy accepts them.";
expectation e_susumu_execution_metadata_stays_declared_until_authenticated target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Execution metadata stays declared until authenticated" detail="Susumu should preserve execution result, exit code, run identity, issuance time, and artifact-manifest references without treating supplied metadata as proof of execution, provenance, retention, or compliance until a configured verifier authenticates it.";
expectation e_susumu_git_signatures_stay_separate_from_execution_proof target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Git signatures stay separate from execution proof" detail="Susumu should reuse Git signature verification to report commit identity and integrity when available, while keeping signature status separate from execution evidence and any conclusion about compliance.";
expectation e_susumu_verification_chains_report_their_trust_boundary target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Verification chains report their trust boundary" detail="Susumu should detect edits, deletions, and reordering in an initialized verification hash chain while clearly reporting that a self-contained chain is not an external trust anchor and cannot by itself resist deliberate rewriting.";
expectation e_susumu_evidence_posture_is_visible_everywhere target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Evidence posture is visible in every review surface" detail="Susumu check JSON, readiness output, and the review portal should expose whether verification evidence is declared, content-bound, execution-declared, or chained, while keeping trust status separate from compliance conclusions.";
expectation e_susumu_dirty_review_propagation target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Changed evidence requests renewed review" detail="When observed code, authored expectations, or links between expectations and work records change, Susumu should clearly flag affected verification and decision records as dirty and request renewed review.";
expectation e_20aaaac113cf6f30 target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Review threads preserve discussion and ownership" detail="Susumu should preserve authored review threads, replies, status, and ownership against stable project, file, symbol, workflow, or expectation targets, and expose them through review artifacts and the portal without treating discussion as verification or approval.";
expectation e_b7a3e3e7205a48a3 target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="TUI exposes review threads and ownership" detail="The engineering TUI should let reviewers browse authored review threads, replies, statuses, and ownership labels while keeping discussion distinct from verification evidence.";
expectation e_a55e93104ffdac81 target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Review links remain explainable" detail="Susumu should flag review threads whose target or parent reply is missing from the current artifact, so discussion never silently loses its evidence anchor.";
expectation e_fa8bd8cf892f2fb0 target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Review thread graphs remain acyclic" detail="Susumu should flag self-parented or cyclic review threads so threaded discussion has a finite, inspectable reply structure.";
expectation e_1b40abd01b1f351e target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Open review threads become actionable work" detail="Susumu should surface open review threads with their owner, target, and next action in the review queue, CLI filters, TUI, and portal.";
expectation e_c370aa74e3d748dd target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Portal review threads can be filtered" detail="The HTML review portal should let business and operations reviewers search and filter review threads by text, owner, and status using the same packet records as the CLI and TUI.";
expectation e_d2ea70fddeae3e96 target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Static portal does not imply mutation" detail="The HTML-only review portal must clearly remain read-only and must not imply that a viewer can reply, assign, resolve, or write project records without a configured authenticated review service.";
expectation e_fb67a766557d0f8d target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Repository-connected review collaboration is auditable" detail="Susumu should let authenticated business and engineering users review multiple connected repositories, persist their actions, and synchronize review changes through an auditable pull-request lifecycle without writing directly from static HTML.";
expectation e_5cb64d62c94d45d1 target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Collaboration preserves compliance evidence posture" detail="Susumu collaboration features must preserve declared, human-reviewed, and authenticated evidence distinctions and must never imply certification, control satisfaction, or compliance approval from comments, attestations, or pull requests alone.";
expectation e_88f8b90833f3a00c target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Feature inventory preserves existing surfaces" detail="Susumu documentation should inventory the current scanner, records, findings, review, Git, compliance, TUI, CLI, CI, JSON, and portal capabilities so new collaboration work does not silently remove or narrow them.";
expectation e_8975f30ee4865f18 target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Shared review API serves every Susumu surface" detail="The live Rust API should expose the same portable project memory used by the CLI, TUI, frontend, and CI, so engineering and business users can collaborate without creating a second evidence model.";
expectation e_b1c5dd37a9811667 target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Dockerized API has a safe operational foundation" detail="Susumu should provide an optional Rust API binary with modular server code, versioned PostgreSQL migrations, health reporting, local user sessions, and a reproducible Docker Compose deployment without changing the default CLI and TUI path.";
expectation e_4f2d7a8c1b6e90d3 target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Repository connections are scoped and auditable" detail="The live API should let administrators register allowlisted repository connections and base branches, persist synchronization state per repository and base branch, and expose those connections only to authenticated Susumu users without accepting arbitrary repository paths or provider credentials from clients.";
expectation e_7b1e4c9d2a6f83e0 target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Sync requests remain repository-scoped" detail="A live synchronization request should validate the configured repository and base branch, transition only that repository/base-branch state, and record the authenticated actor before any provider or pull-request work begins.";
expectation e_3d8a1f6c4b9e20d7 target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="GitHub App credentials remain server-side" detail="GitHub App identity and private-key material should be loaded only from server deployment configuration, validated before use, and kept out of browser responses, database records, and portable Susumu evidence.";
expectation e_8c2f5a1d7b9e40f6 target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Repository inspection stays allowlisted" detail="Provider-backed repository inspection should use only the configured repository and base branches, return source-control identifiers without credentials, and reject arbitrary repository paths or branches.";
expectation e_6d2f8a1c9b4e3075 target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Repository synchronization has one active PR lifecycle" detail="For each connected repository, synchronization should claim at most one active lifecycle, materialize only configured Susumu sidecars, reuse the active pull request while it is pending, and start a new lifecycle only after the prior one is marked merged.";
expectation e_9a4c1e7d2b6f3085 target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Live frontend keeps collaboration understandable" detail="The optional authenticated frontend should give business and engineering users a calm same-origin workspace for login, connected repository posture, administrator registration, and bounded Susumu sidecar submission without exposing provider credentials or implying unsupported review or compliance capabilities.";
expectation e_6f3a9c1d7b5e2048 target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Business users can author project memory without raw syntax" detail="The authenticated frontend should let business and engineering users add expectations, verifications, work records, and review comments through guided forms while preserving the same portable records and repository-scoped pull-request lifecycle used by the CLI, TUI, and CI.";
expectation e_7a4c1e9d5b2f3086 target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Portal sessions and evidence drill-down survive refresh" detail="The authenticated portal should restore a valid session after refresh, show repository records consistently, support fuzzy search and full record detail, and make timeline, source context, and next work visible without exposing raw sidecar syntax.";
expectation e_8b5d2f1a7c9e4063 target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Workspace errors do not masquerade as logout" detail="After the portal authenticates a user, failures loading repository data should preserve the authenticated workspace and explain the data-loading problem instead of incorrectly returning the user to the login screen.";
expectation e_4f8b2c1d6a9e3075 target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Record details preserve anchored conversations" detail="When a user opens an expectation, verification, or work record, Susumu should show its anchored review threads, nested replies, ownership, and actions to start or continue a discussion through the CLI, TUI, live portal, and exported evidence model.";
expectation e_5a9c3f7b1d60482 target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Search scales with project memory" detail="Authenticated portal and API clients should search indexed Susumu record summaries with ranked fuzzy matching, project and branch scope, filters, pagination, and refresh behavior that reflects repository additions, updates, and removals without loading raw sidecars into the browser.";
expectation e_6b2d8f4a1c90735e target=project subject=- status=proposed source="human:owner" title="Repository synchronization preserves provenance and user-controlled conflicts" detail="Each repository synchronization records the base and active head commit SHAs, detects base-branch advancement, and gives users an explicit safe update path without silently overwriting conflicting work.";
expectation e_7c3d9a1f5b2e4087 target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:owner" title="Susumu can be tested locally and deployed cross-platform" detail="Susumu should provide clear, platform-neutral instructions for running the complete Docker Compose stack locally and deploying it with persistent PostgreSQL, HTTPS, secrets, backups, and administrator-owned GitHub configuration on Linux, macOS, or Windows-compatible container infrastructure.";
expectation e_8d4e1a7c2b9f3056 target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:owner" title="The live API fails predictably under operational pressure" detail="The optional API should bound external and database operations, shut down gracefully, stop background refresh work, and preserve safe behavior when dependencies or the process are interrupted.";
expectation e_9f5c2a7d1b4e3086 target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:owner" title="Source history remains comparable across migrations" detail="Susumu should record the source-control revision of each scan and identify exact or candidate mappings for files, symbols, and workflows that move or change across Git revisions, without silently rewriting authored evidence.";
expectation e_a6d2f8c4b1e90735 target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:owner" title="Changed source makes dependent review visibly dirty" detail="When source identities migrate or review context changes, Susumu should identify affected expectations, verifications, decisions, work records, and review anchors with an actionable explanation without silently retargeting authored records.";
expectation e_b8f4c2d1a907356 target=project subject=- status=proposed source="human:owner" title="Source migrations can be resolved explicitly" detail="Susumu should show source migration candidates and let a reviewer explicitly accept, reject, or defer each mapping, preserving an auditable record without silently rewriting authored evidence.";
